<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#080b18">
<meta name="description" content="Read Campusora's Privacy Policy to understand how we collect, use, protect and manage your personal information.">

<title>Privacy Policy | Campusora</title>

<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

<style>
:root {
  --bg:#080b18;
  --card:#111629;
  --border:rgba(255,255,255,.08);
  --text:#f4f5ff;
  --muted:#a0a9c2;
  --purple:#925bff;
  --blue:#526dff;
  --cyan:#39d7f5;
}

* {
  box-sizing:border-box;
  margin:0;
  padding:0;
}

body {
  background:var(--bg);
  color:var(--text);
  font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;
  min-height:100vh;
  line-height:1.8;
}

a {
  color:#a99aff;
  text-decoration:none;
}

a:hover {
  text-decoration:underline;
}

.container {
  width:min(850px,92%);
  margin:35px auto 70px;
}

.brand {
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  gap:10px;
  margin-bottom:30px;
  font-size:21px;
  font-weight:800;
}

.brand span {
  color:var(--cyan);
}

.heading {
  margin-bottom:25px;
}

.tag {
  display:inline-block;
  padding:6px 12px;
  border-radius:30px;
  background:rgba(146,91,255,.13);
  border:1px solid rgba(146,91,255,.25);
  color:#c9b8ff;
  font-size:10px;
  font-weight:800;
  margin-bottom:12px;
}

h1 {
  font-size:clamp(28px,5vw,39px);
  letter-spacing:-1px;
  line-height:1.25;
  margin-bottom:10px;
}

.updated {
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:12px;
}

.intro {
  background:linear-gradient(120deg,rgba(146,91,255,.15),rgba(57,215,245,.07));
  border:1px solid rgba(146,91,255,.2);
  border-radius:17px;
  padding:22px;
  margin-bottom:25px;
  color:#dce1f5;
  font-size:13px;
}

.section {
  background:var(--card);
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:15px;
  padding:21px;
  margin-bottom:14px;
}

.section h2 {
  font-size:16px;
  margin-bottom:10px;
  color:#fff;
}

.section p {
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:12.5px;
  margin-bottom:10px;
}

.section p:last-child {
  margin-bottom:0;
}

.section ul {
  padding-left:19px;
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:12.5px;
}

.section li {
  margin-bottom:7px;
}

.notice {
  background:rgba(57,215,245,.06);
  border:1px solid rgba(57,215,245,.18);
  border-radius:13px;
  padding:17px;
  color:#c5eaf3;
  font-size:12px;
  margin-top:20px;
}

.contact {
  margin-top:22px;
  padding:22px;
  border-radius:15px;
  background:linear-gradient(120deg,rgba(146,91,255,.16),rgba(57,215,245,.08));
  border:1px solid rgba(146,91,255,.2);
}

.contact h2 {
  font-size:17px;
  margin-bottom:8px;
}

.contact p {
  color:var(--muted);
  font-size:12.5px;
  margin-bottom:12px;
}

.contact a {
  display:inline-block;
  margin:5px 12px 5px 0;
  font-size:12px;
  font-weight:700;
}

.footer {
  text-align:center;
  color:#737e9b;
  font-size:11px;
  margin-top:30px;
}

@media(max-width:600px) {
  .container {
    margin-top:23px;
  }

  .section {
    padding:17px;
  }

  .intro {
    padding:18px;
  }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<main class="container">

  <div class="brand">
    Campus<span>ora</span>
  </div>

  <header class="heading">
    <span class="tag">YOUR PRIVACY MATTERS</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 18 November 2026</p>
  </header>

  <div class="intro">
    Campusora respects your privacy. This policy explains
    what information we collect, how we use it, when it may
    be shared and the choices available to you when using
    the Campusora social platform.
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>1. About Campusora</h2>
    <p>
      Campusora is a social platform designed to connect
      students, alumni and general members across Nigerian
      campuses and communities.
    </p>
    <p>
      Through Campusora, members can create profiles,
      publish posts, share media, communicate, discover
      communities, explore opportunities and use other
      platform features.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on how you use Campusora, we may collect
      the following categories of information:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information:</strong>
        Information such as your email address and
        authentication details when you register or log in.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Profile information:</strong>
        Your name, username, profile picture, cover photo,
        institution, membership type, biography and other
        details you choose to provide.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Content and activity:</strong>
        Posts, comments, reactions, uploaded photos,
        videos, stories, marketplace listings and other
        content you create or share.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Communications:</strong>
        Messages, call-related information and interactions
        made through Campusora's communication features.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Transaction information:</strong>
        Payment references, transaction amounts and
        payment status associated with purchases,
        subscriptions or promotions.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Device and technical information:</strong>
        Information needed to operate the platform,
        maintain sessions, troubleshoot problems and
        support notifications.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Notification information:</strong>
        Device notification subscription details when
        you give permission to receive push notifications.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use information to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Create and manage member accounts.</li>
      <li>Display profiles and connect members.</li>
      <li>Operate posts, comments, messages and communities.</li>
      <li>Deliver notifications you have enabled.</li>
      <li>Process and verify payments and purchases.</li>
      <li>Manage promotions and marketplace activities.</li>
      <li>Improve platform performance and user experience.</li>
      <li>Detect abuse, fraud, spam and security problems.</li>
      <li>Respond to support requests and enforce platform rules.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>4. Public Content and Visibility</h2>
    <p>
      Campusora is a social platform. Information you
      publish publicly may be visible to other members
      and, where accessible without signing in, people
      outside Campusora.
    </p>
    <p>
      This may include your public profile details,
      posts, comments, uploaded media and other
      interactions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please think carefully before sharing personal
      information publicly. Other people may copy,
      screenshot or share content you publish.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>5. Private Messages and Communications</h2>
    <p>
      Messages sent through Campusora are intended for
      the participants in the relevant conversation.
    </p>
    <p>
      We process communication information to operate
      messaging, deliver notifications, maintain platform
      security and support the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not share passwords, financial credentials or
      other highly sensitive information in messages.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>6. Payments and Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      Campusora uses third-party service providers to
      operate certain platform features.
    </p>
    <p>
      These include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Supabase:</strong>
        Used for account authentication, database
        services and related platform infrastructure.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Vercel:</strong>
        Used to host and deliver parts of the platform.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Paystack:</strong>
        Used to process payments where supported.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Payments are handled through the payment provider.
      Campusora may receive transaction references,
      amounts, payment status and related information
      needed to verify purchases.
    </p>
    <p>
      Third-party providers process information under
      their own applicable privacy policies and terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>7. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
    <p>
      Campusora may use browser storage and similar
      technologies to keep you signed in, remember
      session information, support platform functions
      and improve your experience.
    </p>
    <p>
      Clearing browser storage may sign you out or
      affect certain platform features.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>8. Push Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      If you allow notifications, Campusora may store
      device subscription information so it can deliver
      relevant messages, calls, activity updates and
      reminders.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can manage notification permission through
      your browser or device settings. Turning off
      notifications may prevent you from receiving
      some updates.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>9. When We Share Information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information.
      We may share information only where reasonably
      necessary, including:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        With service providers that help operate
        Campusora.
      </li>
      <li>
        With payment providers to process transactions.
      </li>
      <li>
        When required by applicable law or a valid
        legal request.
      </li>
      <li>
        To protect members, investigate abuse or
        protect the security of the platform.
      </li>
      <li>
        When you choose to share information or
        interact with other members.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>10. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use technical and organisational measures
      intended to protect information against
      unauthorised access, loss, misuse or disclosure.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, no online service or method of
      electronic storage can be guaranteed to be
      completely secure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>11. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain information for as long as reasonably
      necessary to operate Campusora, provide services,
      maintain security, resolve disputes and meet
      applicable legal obligations.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some information may remain in backups or records
      for a limited period after an account or content
      removal request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>12. Your Privacy Choices and Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on applicable law, you may have rights
      to request access to, correction of, deletion of
      or information about the personal data we hold
      about you.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also manage certain profile details,
      content and notification permissions through
      available Campusora features and your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      To make a privacy request, contact us using
      the details below. We may need to verify your
      identity before responding.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some privacy settings within the platform may
      not yet apply to every feature. Do not rely on
      a setting to restrict access to content unless
      the relevant feature clearly confirms that
      restriction.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>13. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Campusora is designed for a broad campus
      community. Anyone who is not legally able to
      consent to the processing of their personal
      information should use the platform only with
      the involvement and permission of a parent
      or legal guardian where required by applicable law.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe a child has provided personal
      information inappropriately, please contact us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>14. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy when our
      services, technology or legal obligations change.
    </p>
    <p>
      Updated versions will be published on this page.
      The date at the top will show when the policy
      was last revised.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>15. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions, concerns or requests
      about this Privacy Policy or how Campusora
      handles personal information, contact us:
    </p>
    <p>
      Email:
      <a href="mailto:ablegodluke@gmail.com">
        ablegodluke@gmail.com
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>
      WhatsApp:
      <a href="https://wa.me/2349017579718"
         target="_blank"
         rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Contact Campusora Support
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="notice">
    By using Campusora, you acknowledge that you have
    had the opportunity to read this Privacy Policy.
    Where consent is required by law, we will seek
    that consent separately.
  </div>

  <footer class="footer">
    © 2026 Campusora. All rights reserved.
    <br>
    Connect. Learn. Grow. Together.
  </footer>

</main>

</body>
</html>
